mode: "100644"
text: "# The FRAME framework — Stories that deepen the relationship\n\nStories aren't disposable filler and they aren't a reach play — they're the **intimate, interactive\nsurface** where your warmest followers give you fast, low-polish attention. FRAME builds a sequence\nthat earns the tap-through, converts watchers into tappers, and drives one clear action.\n\n## F — First frame earns the tap-through\n- Open with a **sound-off hook** stating the problem or outcome (most exits happen on frame 1).\n- 9:16, key content in the **safe zone**, **text sparingly**, on-brand. One reason to stay.\n\n## R — Rhythm: one beat per frame\n- Build a **3–5 frame arc** (or a multi-day mini-series); **one beat per frame**, each a distinct\n  takeaway, building progressively. Segments can run to 60s, but a short beat (~15s) holds attention.\n- Vary the frames (photo, clip, text card) so it doesn't feel like one flat slideshow.\n\n## A — Activate with a sticker\n- Add an **interactive sticker** — the single most effective Stories tool. Pick by goal: **poll/slider**\n  (feedback), **quiz** (educate/segment), **question box** (AMA → DMs), **countdown** (real deadline).\n- Each tap is a **relationship signal** and free audience research.\n\n## M — Move to one action\n- **One goal per sequence.** If the goal is replies → a question. If a link click → problem → solution\n  → **link sticker + \"Tap here\" overlay** at the end. If engagement → poll/quiz before the payoff.\n- Don't ask viewers to do three things; the clearer the single action, the stronger the result.\n\n## E — Evergreen the winners + engage the replies\n- **Highlight** proven sequences (with context) so an ephemeral surface gets an evergreen tail.\n- **DM every reply** personally — that conversation is the real relationship (and a strong signal).\n- Read **completion / exits / sticker taps** natively to learn which arcs and stickers land; repeat\n  the winners.\n\n## The Story brief a request should fill\n```\nGOAL (one): replies | link click | profile visit | poll feedback\nARC: 3–5 frames, one beat each; F1 = sound-off hook (problem/outcome)\nFRAMES: copy per frame (brand voice), sound-off legible, safe zone\nSTICKER: which one + exact copy (poll/quiz/question/countdown/link)\nACTION: the single next step + \"Tap here\" overlay if a link\nAFTER: Highlight if it's evergreen; DM-reply plan\n```\n"
